GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> ;
    narr:childCount "47"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "f58158f50ab61ca1389fbda1692db84740721302" ;
    narr:narration """This narrative records a team-owner ruling on reaction delivery, re-recorded across six dated passes and extended once. [The framing of where reaction delivery belongs](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_1) grounds [the directive that every reaction routes through one bundle per run per person, not one message per skill](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_2), held under [pushback on the batching window, answered by the rule that a bundle closes when the run closes and a late skill waits for the next run](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_3), with [per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing rejected as moving the ordering problem onto the reader](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_4) — [that rejection also stated separately](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5). Earlier passes re-record the same arc as [framing](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_1), [directive](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), [pushback exchange](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3), and [rejected alternative](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4); a second pass as [framing](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_1), [directive](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_2), [pushback](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_3), and [alternative](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_4); a third as [framing](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_1), [directive](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_2), [pushback](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_3), and [alternative](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_4); a fourth as [framing](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_1), [directive](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_2), [pushback](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_3), and [alternative](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_4); and a fifth as [framing](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_1), [directive](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_2), [pushback](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_3), and [alternative](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_4). A second layer extends it: [the framing of how the week's reactions reach people](narr:Expr_20260925_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h5c24fdddd3e5_1) grounds [keeping the per-run bundle and adding one Friday roll-up of the week](narr:Expr_20260925_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h5c24fdddd3e5_2), with [the reported question on whether the roll-up replaces the bundle](narr:Expr_20260925_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h5c24fdddd3e5_3) answered by [the scope clarification that the bundle is for the run, the roll-up for the week](narr:Expr_20260925_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h5c24fdddd3e5_4) and [the rejection of a daily digest as repeating the bundle word for word](narr:Expr_20260925_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h5c24fdddd3e5_5); a later pass re-records that layer as [framing](narr:Expr_20260927_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_hf65a0248bea8_1), [directive](narr:Expr_20260927_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_hf65a0248bea8_2), [question](narr:Expr_20260927_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_hf65a0248bea8_3), [clarification](narr:Expr_20260927_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_hf65a0248bea8_4), and [rejection](narr:Expr_20260927_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_hf65a0248bea8_5); and a sixth as [framing](narr:Expr_20260929_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h94add5a10097_1), [directive](narr:Expr_20260929_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h94add5a10097_2), [question](narr:Expr_20260929_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h94add5a10097_3), [clarification](narr:Expr_20260929_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h94add5a10097_4), and [rejection](narr:Expr_20260929_1_WeeklyRollUpRulingE2EAgenticSynthetic_h94add5a10097_5). A seventh pass re-records the routing arc as [framing](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_2), [directive](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_3), [the reported pushback on the batching window](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_4), [the held rule that the bundle closes when the run closes](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_5), and [the rejected per-skill alternative](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_6). The arc supports [the position on where bundling and batching windows should be bounded](narr:Position_ReactionDeliveryBundlingAndBatchingBoundary) and [the position on scheduling recurring reaction summaries alongside per-run bundles](narr:Position_WeeklyReactionRollUpCadence). The register across the ruling quotes runs antithesis and parallelism — one thing to read, not four.""" ;
    narr:reaction """One sentence arrived and one arc gained a member: the seventh pass ([the 20260930 re-recording](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_2)) now sits in the narration, and it is structurally the finest-grained yet — where earlier passes folded the pushback exchange into one statement, this pass splits [Tina's reported pushback](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_4) from [Tanya's held rule](narr:Expr_20260930_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h8da21f01f22b_5), which is why the first variation line now anchors the split rather than the merged form. Nothing else moved: the two positions, the weekly-roll-up layer, and the register note all held byte for byte.""" ;
